[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every date-swap report into one ticket and called it known:
one parser bug, one fix queued. Reading every merged report's body shows that's three problems,
not one.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471's own cause table already renders this: the <code>hint</code> row shows "not this ticket
— no ticket of its own." This page adds the third problem the mechanical grouping cannot see.
</Callout>

## What #4471 actually holds

<BreakdownTable ticket={4471} />

- **parser** — the shared parser reads every date month first; day-first tenants (by
  `Intl.DateTimeFormat`, see `causes.ts: dayFirst()`) get it flipped. This is #4471's real bug.
- **hint** — `booking-v3`'s own `MM/DD` hint causes the opposite flip on day-first tenants who
  type what the hint tells them. Same user-visible symptom, different code path, no ticket.
- **day/timezone boundary** — five reports (`desk-notes.json: oneDayMove`) read, body by body,
  as a one-day or cross-timezone shift: "every booking in June is one day off," two attendees
  in different cities seeing different weekdays for the same meeting, an invite that "arrived
  before I made the booking." None of the five mention a swapped day/month pair. `causeOf()`
  never reads report text, so it files all five under `parser` by tenant+channel; they are not
  that bug.

## Why this matters

A ticket that is "known" because its headline count and its biggest cause agree can still hide
a second cause with no ticket, and a third with no cause bucket at all. The numbers above are
computed from the same `reports-4471.json`/`desk-notes.json` this export shipped with — nothing
here is typed into the page.

## What to do

File the `hint` and `day/timezone boundary` reports as their own tickets; leave #4471 as the
parser ticket it actually is, now at its real count.

